\begin{center}
Review of final report: \\
International Research Training Group \\
DROPIT: ``Droplet Interaction Technologies \\
Lead PIs: \\
Dr. Bernhard Weigant University of Stuttgart \\
Dr. Gianpietro Elvio Cossali  University of Bergamo \\
\today  \\
\end{center}
As quoted from the final report:
``The research of DROPIT had been organised in three
thematic areas (TA): TA-A: Drop-Gas Interaction, 
TA-B: Drop-Wall Interaction, TA-C: Drop-Liquid Interaction.''  
\par\noindent
The results of this study have many applications: atomization and spray
in internal combustion engines, aircraft icing, sloshing in cryogenic
fuel tanks, nuclear reactor cooling systems, microfluidic devices, 
additive manufacturing, hydraulic fracturing, spray cooling,
medical inhalers, human perspiration, PEM fuel cells, membrane
emulsification and filtration, thermal insulation, 
air-conditioning of buildings, distribution of plant protection
agents, coating processes, gluing, fire suppression,
medical sprays, 
shelf life of food, asphalt preservation, biomass,
ceramic green bodies, soil erosion, encapsulation technologies,
and the design of ``breathable'' fabrics.
\par\noindent
I find that all of the published articles and PhD Thesis, that were supported
by way of the DFG ``Dropit'' program,  make important
contributions towards furthering our understanding of the 
fundamental mechanisms governing multiphase and multiphysics
flows in general, and droplet
technologies in particular.  I highlight below some
of the research here which report on 
studies in which recent experimental results
were compared to novel simulations and mathematical modeling.
\begin{itemize}
\item Palmetshofer, P., Saha, R., Bryce, J., Geppert, A., 
Cossali, G.E., Weigand, B., 2025. Droplet impact onto 
sub-millimeter microstructures fully and barely submerged in a liquid film.
Phys. Fluids 37, 082130.
\item Palmetshofer, P., Wurst, J., Geppert, A., Schulte, K., Cossali, G.E., Weigand, B., 2025. Wetting
behavior in the inertial phase of droplet impacts onto sub-millimeter microstructured surfaces. Journal
of Colloid and Interface Science 682, 413–422. 
\item Palmetshofer, P., Geppert, A., Steigerwald, J., Arcos Marz, T., Weigand, B., 2024. Thermocapillary
central lamella recess during droplet impacts onto a heated wall. Sci Rep 14, 1102.
\item Schubert, S., Steigerwald, J., Geppert, A., 
Weigand, B., Lamanna, G., 2024. Micro-PIV study on the
influence of viscosity on the dynamics of droplet 
impact onto a thin film. Exp Fluids 65, 69.
\item Geppert, A., Stober, J., Steigerwald, J., Schulte, K., Tonini, S., 
Lamanna, G., 2024. Analyzing the early impact dynamics of single 
droplets impacting onto wetted surfaces. Phys.  Fluids 36, 012005.
\item Veyskarami, M., Bringedal, C., Helmig, R., 2024. Modeling and 
Analysis of Droplet Evaporation at the Interface of a Coupled 
Free-Flow-Porous Medium System. Transp Porous Med 151, 2745–2775.
\item Ackermann, S., Fest-Santini, S., Veyskarami, M., Helmig, R., 
Santini, M., 2023. Experimental validation of a coupling 
concept for drop formation and growth onto porous materials 
by high-resolution X-ray imaging technique. Int J Multiphas Flow 160, 104371. 
\item Lamanna, G., Geppert, A., Bernard, R., Weigand, B., 2022. 
 Drop impact onto wetted walls: an unsteady analytical 
 solution for modelling crown spreading. J. Fluid Mech. 938, A34.
\item Michalkowski, C., Veyskarami, M., Bringedal, C., Helmig, R., 
Schleper, V., 2022. Two-phase Flow Dynamics at the Interface Between 
